   "user": {
    "name": "Michael Barton",
    "link": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110063207238250789189?hl=en-US",
    "contributor_id": "110063207238250789189",
    "thumbnail": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVY_f0SsmBebSzTk4iRa30Rm9yj3OfHp9LWA-M_30-k5NMY30djKg=s120-c-rp-mo-ba12-br100",
    "local_guide": true,
    "reviews": 1830,
    "photos": 9783
   },
   "snippet": "As far as upper level BBQ goes, the meats here are mid. However, the sides are fantastic! If you compare Stiles Switch to general BBQ then the meat cuts are wonderful and the sides are absolutely phenomenal.\n\nThe classic red meats here are lower tier 2, upper tier 3. The brisket I had was half dry, half fatty with no consistency. The ribs were good enough but I couldn't tell you anything in depth about their flavors. The turkey was best because it was juicy and very well marinade. The sides, especially the corn casserole, were great and I'd eat them any time. Weirdly, the house mustard was by far the best thing and is nearly drinkable.",
   "extracted_snippet": {
    "original": "As far as upper level BBQ goes, the meats here are mid. However, the sides are fantastic! If you compare Stiles Switch to general BBQ then the meat cuts are wonderful and the sides are absolutely phenomenal.\n\nThe classic red meats here are lower tier 2, upper tier 3. The brisket I had was half dry, half fatty with no consistency. The ribs were good enough but I couldn't tell you anything in depth about their flavors. The turkey was best because it was juicy and very well marinade. The sides, especially the corn casserole, were great and I'd eat them any time. Weirdly, the house mustard was by far the best thing and is nearly drinkable."
   },
